# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AWS CardDemo — Java 25 / Spring Boot 3.x / Maven migration — VCS ignore rules
#
# Scope notes (see AAP §0.2.1, §0.3.1):
#   * This file ONLY ignores generated build output, IDE/editor metadata, OS
#     cruft, local secrets, and test/scan artifacts.
#   * It MUST NOT ignore committed project assets: pom.xml, the Maven wrapper
#     (mvnw, mvnw.cmd, .mvn/wrapper/*), src/**, docs/**, .github/**, Dockerfile,
#     docker-compose.yml, README.md, LICENSE, NOTICE, diagrams/**, samples/**,
#     the retained legacy COBOL tree (app/** / legacy/**), and the fixed-width
#     parity fixtures under app/data/** (e.g. *.txt, *.PS). No broad *.txt,
#     *.dat, or data/ patterns are used, by design.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ===== Maven build output =====
target/
pom.xml.tag
pom.xml.releaseBackup
pom.xml.versionsBackup
pom.xml.next
release.properties
dependency-reduced-pom.xml
.flattened-pom.xml
buildNumber.properties
# Develocity / Gradle-Enterprise build cache that some Maven setups drop under
# .mvn — ignore only the cache, never the committed wrapper files in .mvn/.
.mvn/.develocity/
.mvn/timing.properties

# ===== Java / JVM artifacts =====
*.class
*.jar
# Re-include the committed Maven wrapper jar (negation MUST follow *.jar so it
# wins under git's last-match rule). .mvn/wrapper/ is never ignored above.
!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
*.war
*.ear
*.nar
*.ctxt
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

# ===== Logs & temp =====
*.log
logs/
*.tmp
*.pid

# ===== Test / coverage / dependency-scan artifacts =====
# JaCoCo & Surefire/Failsafe output normally lands under target/ (already
# ignored); these patterns make intent explicit and also catch output that a
# plugin is configured to write elsewhere.
**/target/site/jacoco/
*.exec
**/jacoco.exec
**/surefire-reports/
**/failsafe-reports/
# OWASP dependency-check report + local NVD data cache.
dependency-check-report.*
dependency-check-data/

# ===== IDE: IntelliJ IDEA =====
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
out/

# ===== IDE: Eclipse =====
.classpath
.project
.settings/
.factorypath
bin/

# ===== IDE: Visual Studio Code =====
.vscode/

# ===== IDE: NetBeans =====
nbproject/
nbbuild/
nbdist/
.nb-gradle/

# ===== IDE: Spring Tool Suite (STS) / Spring Boot annotation processing =====
# Part of the canonical Spring Initializr ignore set for the Spring Boot stack
# used here. These never match committed sources under src/**, legacy/**,
# samples/**, docs/**, or pom.xml — they are IDE/APT scratch output only.
.apt_generated/
.apt_generated_test/
.sts4-cache/
.springBeans

# ===== Editor swap / backup files =====
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ===== OS noise =====
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ===== Local environment / secrets (never commit) =====
# Externalized datasource passwords & seed credentials (AAP §0.6.6) live here.
# The committed application.yml / application-test.yml are NOT matched below.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local
application-local.yml
application-local.properties

# ===== Docker local volumes =====
# The shipped docker-compose.yml uses a Docker-managed named volume, but a
# bind-mounted local PostgreSQL data dir (if introduced) must not be committed.
pgdata/
